.TH COMMANDO 1 2026-10-07 "commando" "User Commands"
.nh
.SH NAME
commando \- a colorful form for any command's options, built from its manual
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B commando
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ command
.RI [ args ...]]
.br
.B commando \-\-explain
.I line
.br
.B commando \-\-init
.I shell
.br
.B commando \-\-completion
.I shell
.br
.B commando \-\-themes
.RI [ name ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B commando
reads a command's manual page, or its
.B \-\-help
output when it has no manual, and shows its options as a form:
checkboxes for flags, dropdowns for options that take one of a set of
values, radio buttons for options that override each other, number and
path fields, and a field for each of the command's arguments.
The side panel explains the focused option.
Press Enter to run the command you built.
.PP
With no
.IR command ,
.B commando
asks which command to run, and lists your recent command lines.
Typing words searches every command line you've run or saved.
.PP
Any
.I args
after the command fill in the form:
.B commando grep \-rn TODO .\&
opens with
.B \-r
and
.B \-n
checked and
.B TODO .\&
as the arguments.
.PP
A tool with subcommands, such as
.BR git ,
.BR docker ,
.B cargo
or
.BR go ,
first lists its commands; choose one to open its form.
.PP
When you press Enter,
.B commando
prints the command and runs it with your
.BR $SHELL .
If it uses an option that can delete or overwrite data, marked with a
warning sign in the form, it asks first.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print
Print the command to standard output instead of running it.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-line " \fIline\fR"
Start from an existing command line.
The shell integration uses this to edit the line you're typing.
.TP
.B \-\-long
Prefer long option names
.RB ( \-\-all )
over short ones
.RB ( \-a ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Read the manual again even if it is cached.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-history
Don't record this command, and don't show presets or recent commands.
.TP
.BI \-\-init " shell"
Print shell integration for
.BR zsh ,
.B bash
or
.BR fish ;
see
.BR "SHELL INTEGRATION" .
.TP
.BI \-\-completion " shell"
Print tab completions for
.BR zsh ,
.B bash
or
.BR fish .
.TP
.B \-\-explain
Describe each option and argument of a command line, from the manuals,
without opening the form.
Pipelines, wrappers such as
.BR sudo ,
variable assignments and redirections are explained too.
A line given as one argument is taken whole:
.B commando \-\-explain \(aqfind . \-name \(dq*.tmp\(dq \-delete\(aq
.TP
.BR \-\-themes " [\fIname\fR ...]"
Show a sample form in each color theme, or only in the themes named
after it.
.TP
.B \-\-config
Show where the settings file is, creating a commented one if there is
none, and check it for mistakes.
.TP
.B \-\-dump
Print the options read from the manual as JSON, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the flags.
.SH KEYS
In the form:
.TP 18
.BR Up ", " Down ", " Tab
Move between fields.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle a checkbox, pick a radio button, open a dropdown.
.TP
.BR Left ", " Right
Cycle dropdown values, turn flags on and off, change a repeat count.
.TP
.BR / ", " Ctrl\-F
Filter the options by name, label or description.
.TP
.BR Ctrl\-O ", " F1 ", " ?
Open the full manual at the focused option.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-X
Show examples from the manual; Enter loads one into the form.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-L
Show presets, recent commands and examples.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-T
Save the form as a named preset.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-S
Switch between short and long option names.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-Y
Copy the command to the clipboard.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-R
Clear the form.
.TP
.B Enter
Run the command, or print it with
.BR \-p .
.TP
.B Esc
Close a dropdown, clear the filter, go back, or quit.
.PP
On the start screen,
.B Ctrl\-D
deletes the chosen saved line or preset, and
.B Ctrl\-Z
puts it back.
In the list of presets and recent commands,
.B Ctrl\-D
deletes the chosen entry.
.SH SHELL INTEGRATION
Add the integration to your shell's startup file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
eval "$(commando \-\-init zsh)"      # ~/.zshrc
eval "$(commando \-\-init bash)"     # ~/.bashrc
commando \-\-init fish | source      # config.fish
.fi
.RE
.PP
Then, while typing a command, press
.B Ctrl\-X Ctrl\-O
to edit it in
.BR commando ;
the result replaces the line on your prompt.
.B Ctrl\-X ?\&
explains the line below the prompt instead.
The bash shortcuts need bash 4 or later.
.PP
Tab completions come the same way, if your package manager didn't install
them:
.PP
.RS
.nf
source <(commando \-\-completion zsh)    # after compinit
source <(commando \-\-completion bash)
commando \-\-completion fish | source
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/commando/config.toml
Settings: preferred option names, whether to confirm risky commands and
keep history, how many recent commands to keep, the color theme, color
overrides, and corrections to what was read from a manual.
.B commando \-\-config
writes a commented one.
.TP
.I ~/.config/commando/store.json
Presets and recent commands on Linux;
.I ~/Library/Application Support/commando/store.json
on macOS.
It holds full command lines, as typed.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/commando
Manuals already read, on Linux;
.I ~/Library/Caches/commando
on macOS.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COMMANDO_CONFIG
The settings file to use.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Where the settings file's folder is, instead of
.IR ~/.config .
.TP
.B COMMANDO_DATA_DIR
The folder for
.IR store.json .
.TP
.B COMMANDO_CACHE_DIR
The folder for cached manuals.
.TP
.B COMMANDO_NO_HISTORY
If set, don't record commands or show presets and history.
.TP
.B COMMANDO_NO_CONFIRM
If set, never ask before running a risky command.
.TP
.B COMMANDO_NO_COMPLETIONS
If set, don't read the shell's completion definitions for dropdown
values.
.TP
.BR COMMANDO_ZSH_COMPLETIONS ", " COMMANDO_FISH_COMPLETIONS
More folders, separated by colons, to read zsh or fish completion
definitions from.
.TP
.B SHELL
The shell that runs the command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of the command that was run;
0 after
.B \-p
prints a command;
130 if you quit without running anything;
2 for a mistake in the flags.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B commando ls
Choose options for
.BR ls ,
then run it.
.TP
.B commando git
Choose a git command, then its options.
.TP
.B cmd=$(commando \-p find)
Build a
.B find
command and keep it in a variable.
.TP
.B commando \-\-explain \(aqtar \-czvf backup.tgz \-\-exclude=.git src\(aq
Say what each part of the line does.
.TP
.B commando \-\-themes nord dracula
Compare two color themes.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR apropos (1)
.PP
https://github.com/lonedevel/commando
